      en: "Piz Medel West is a 3,210 m peak in the Adula Alps, canton of Graubünden, Switzerland. It forms the western part of the Piz Medel massif, noted for its distinctive double summit. The mountain is composed mainly of crystalline rocks such as gneiss and mica schist. The western flank features steep ice and snowfields, used as climbing routes in summer. The area is part of Parc Ela, the largest nature park in Switzerland. The summit offers excellent views of the Rheinwald valley and the Bergell mountains. First ascent was in 1865 by J. J. Weilenmann and a guide. The normal route crosses the Medel Glacier and requires glacier experience.",
